1
00:00:00,650 --> 00:00:04,970
What is the best way to improve your vocabulary?

2
00:00:04,970 --> 00:00:09,929
If you ask this question to English teachers
or other English learners, they will tell

3
00:00:09,929 --> 00:00:11,490
you the same thing.

4
00:00:11,490 --> 00:00:16,779
They'll tell you that the best way to build
your vocabulary is to learn vocabulary in

5
00:00:16,779 --> 00:00:20,130
context by listening and reading a lot.

6
00:00:20,130 --> 00:00:22,250
And I completely agree with that.

7
00:00:22,250 --> 00:00:25,779
That is the best way to increase your vocabulary.

8
00:00:25,779 --> 00:00:27,410
So this is common sense, right?

9
00:00:27,410 --> 00:00:28,919
Everybody knows that.

10
00:00:28,919 --> 00:00:31,329
This topic is so boring.

11
00:00:31,329 --> 00:00:33,370
But there's a problem.

12
00:00:33,370 --> 00:00:36,540
Common sense is not common action.

13
00:00:36,540 --> 00:00:42,070
Everybody knows how to improve their vocabulary,
but most people don't do it.

14
00:00:42,070 --> 00:00:47,420
Because they spend too much time on things
like social media and funny cat videos.

15
00:00:47,420 --> 00:00:54,130
Now, if regular listening and reading is a
common practice for you, then congratulations.

16
00:00:54,130 --> 00:00:55,900
You don't need to watch this video.

17
00:00:55,900 --> 00:01:01,480
But if it's not a common practice for you
yet, let me convince you to start listening

18
00:01:01,480 --> 00:01:04,390
and reading on a regular basis.

19
00:01:10,160 --> 00:01:11,660
So let's get stared.

20
00:01:11,660 --> 00:01:15,270
The first benefit you'll get is "intuition."

21
00:01:15,270 --> 00:01:16,700
What is intuition?

22
00:01:16,700 --> 00:01:22,220
Well, let's say that you come across a multiple
choice question about English grammar.

23
00:01:22,220 --> 00:01:27,410
You look at the choices and you know immediately
what the correct answer is.

24
00:01:27,410 --> 00:01:29,890
You don't know the grammar rule that explains
it.

25
00:01:29,890 --> 00:01:31,810
There's no reasoning behind it.

26
00:01:31,810 --> 00:01:33,550
It just feels right.

27
00:01:33,550 --> 00:01:35,400
That's intuition.

28
00:01:35,400 --> 00:01:40,270
It comes from taking in a lot of input by
listening and reading.

29
00:01:40,270 --> 00:01:44,750
Unfortunately, some people don't appreciate
the power of intuition.

30
00:01:44,750 --> 00:01:49,000
They learn vocabulary in a very strange way.

31
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:50,810
They don't learn words in context.

32
00:01:50,810 --> 00:01:57,810
Instead, they find a list of words and memorize
the meaning of each word one by one.

33
00:01:58,460 --> 00:02:00,200
This seems like a good idea.

34
00:02:00,200 --> 00:02:03,449
They're learning a lot of new words in a short
period of time.

35
00:02:03,449 --> 00:02:06,390
There's only one problem with this.

36
00:02:06,390 --> 00:02:08,050
It's stupid.

37
00:02:08,050 --> 00:02:11,750
Just because we know the meaning of a word
doesn't mean that we can use it.

38
00:02:11,750 --> 00:02:13,159
It's not enough.

39
00:02:13,159 --> 00:02:16,080
We also need to know how the word is used.

40
00:02:16,080 --> 00:02:18,580
Now, I'm sure that you already know this,
right?

41
00:02:18,580 --> 00:02:20,429
You're not one of those people.

42
00:02:20,429 --> 00:02:26,409
You already know that it's much better to
learn vocabulary by listening and reading.

43
00:02:26,409 --> 00:02:32,030
Because when you do that, you're not only
improving your vocabulary but also grammar,

44
00:02:32,030 --> 00:02:34,069
sentence structure, and so on.

45
00:02:34,069 --> 00:02:38,140
Over time, you will become an independent
learner.

46
00:02:38,140 --> 00:02:43,580
It means that you'll have the ability to improve
your English without help from other people.

47
00:02:43,580 --> 00:02:45,879
And that's really cool.

48
00:02:45,879 --> 00:02:49,170
Let's talk about the second benefit of this
habit.

49
00:02:49,170 --> 00:02:53,220
The second benefit is an increase in brain
power.

50
00:02:53,220 --> 00:02:58,890
Just like how a muscle needs physical exercise
to become stronger, your brain needs mental

51
00:02:58,890 --> 00:03:01,429
exercise to grow as well.

52
00:03:01,429 --> 00:03:05,439
Regular listening and reading is a great mental
exercise.

53
00:03:05,439 --> 00:03:08,179
It improves so many functions of the brain.

54
00:03:08,179 --> 00:03:12,099
When you listen to someone speaking, you have
to stay focused.

55
00:03:12,099 --> 00:03:14,129
This improves your attention.

56
00:03:14,129 --> 00:03:19,119
And if they're speaking really fast, you're
also training your brain to process information

57
00:03:19,119 --> 00:03:22,819
faster, which leads to better comprehension.

58
00:03:22,819 --> 00:03:24,349
Reading is great too.

59
00:03:24,349 --> 00:03:26,329
It improves your memory.

60
00:03:26,329 --> 00:03:31,679
When you read a novel, you need to remember
lots of details like the names of the characters,

61
00:03:31,679 --> 00:03:35,069
their backgrounds, the plot, and so on.

62
00:03:35,069 --> 00:03:37,689
Some books even increase your intelligence.

63
00:03:37,689 --> 00:03:41,189
Reading certain types of books improves the
way you think.

64
00:03:41,189 --> 00:03:43,039
And these are just a few benefits.

65
00:03:43,039 --> 00:03:47,039
There are so many other benefits that I didn't
even mention here.

66
00:03:47,039 --> 00:03:52,099
Now you might be thinking, "Why should I care
about my brain power?"

67
00:03:52,099 --> 00:03:57,469
Well, because it will play a huge role in
your English language development.

68
00:03:57,469 --> 00:04:00,969
Especially if you're trying to improve your
spoken English.

69
00:04:00,969 --> 00:04:07,069
For non-native English speakers like you and
I, speaking English requires a lot of effort.

70
00:04:07,069 --> 00:04:13,570
It places great demands on so many cognitive
functions like memory, attention, auditory

71
00:04:13,570 --> 00:04:15,919
processing, reasoning, and so on.

72
00:04:15,919 --> 00:04:21,060
So if you want to speak English well, you're
going to need to have a strong, healthy brain

73
00:04:21,060 --> 00:04:22,780
with lots of power.

74
00:04:22,780 --> 00:04:28,190
And by the way, if you're not living in an
English-speaking country, this habit is a

75
00:04:28,190 --> 00:04:28,639
must.

76
00:04:28,639 --> 00:04:33,079
And I'm speaking from my personal experience
here because I've never been to an English-speaking

77
00:04:33,079 --> 00:04:34,049
country.

78
00:04:34,049 --> 00:04:38,979
If you're in the same situation, the only
way for you to immerse yourself in the English

79
00:04:38,979 --> 00:04:43,419
language is by applying this simple but powerful
habit.

80
00:04:43,419 --> 00:04:46,440
I guarantee that you'll love the results.

